# RStudio Connect folder
rsconnect/

# Reference TR catalogues downloaded from UCSC / TRExplorer / STRchive, and the
# index caches built beside them (30 MB+ blobs that `uv run novelty` and
# `python -m strchive` re-fetch on demand, so they should not land in a commit)
data/reference/

# Index caches the novelty screen builds beside a catalogue it is pointed at.
# The downloaded catalogues live under data/reference/ above, but the in-repo
# pathogenic BED is screened in place, so its sidecar lands in data/novelty/.
*.idx.npz

# Results fetched off a DNAnexus worker by scripts/dnanexus/dx-instance.sh.
# They are on the platform too (under /Results/<you>/), which is where they
# belong.
data/dx/

# Fetched reference catalogs for the web layer. Regenerate with
# `cd backend && uv run python scripts/fetch_strchive.py`. The manifest that
# describes this file IS committed (data/web/strchive-loci.yaml); the data is a
# pinned, checksummed download, so it is not.
data/web/strchive/

# The real callsets and the loci/segments tables built from them - hprc (67
# unrelated genomes) and trio (GIAB HG002/03/04). The manifests that describe
# them ARE committed (data/web/hprc-*.yaml, data/web/trio-*.yaml); the data is
# somebody else's cohort, so it is fetched and rebuilt rather than cloned:
#   just plot-data && just plot-parquet && just strchive-data && just web-data
# See data/web/README.md for what each step is for.
data/web/hprc_multisample.trf.noveltyFiltered.tsv
data/hprc/
data/trio/
# Inputs and outputs of the plotting scripts in src/R/plotting/ - the numbered
# tables (02_ novelty-filtered calls, 03_ catalogue membership, 04_ AnnotSV
# annotation, 05_ the merge main.R writes). They are 165 MB+ of derived pipeline
# output, so they are regenerated or downloaded rather than cloned - see
# docs/analysis/PLOTTING.md for what each one is and where it comes from.
data/plots/

# Files handed to the web interface through the Upload button, plus the
# manifests generated for them. Somebody else's callset is exactly the thing
# that should not ride along in a clone; the directory itself is kept so the
# bind mount has something to attach to.
data/uploads/*
!data/uploads/.gitkeep
data/web/upload-*.yaml

#### NEXTFLOW PIPELINE

# Large input/output data - regenerated by running the pipeline, or
# fetched separately (see data/dx/ note above for the DNAnexus
# equivalent of this same idea)
data/*.vcf
data/*.vcf.gz
results/
# ...except the population-structure analysis outputs, which are tracked and
# small (see docs/analysis/POPULATION_STRUCTURE.md). Nextflow writes its own
# run outputs elsewhere under results/, and those stay ignored.
!results/
results/*
!results/figures/
results/figures/*
!results/figures/*.pdf
!results/locus_carriers.tsv
!results/locus_carriers_full.tsv
!results/per_sample_insertion_burden.tsv

# Nextflow run artifacts - logs, work directory, session cache
.nextflow/
.nextflow.log*
work/

# Run reports configured in nextflow.config (timeline/report/trace/dag)
reports/

#### BUILT BINARIES

# Third-party JARs. htsSidra is built from source at
# https://github.com/idraktt/qgp_sv_paper/tree/main/htsSidra (see
# pipelines/annotate_from_bed/HOW-TO.md); an 11 MB fat jar has no business in a
# clone when `mvn package` reproduces it from a pinned upstream commit.
*.jar

# Generated figure rasters (PDFs are tracked)
results/figures/*.png

# Akshay's filtered call set (55 MB) lives on DNAnexus under
# Results/NoveltyFiltering_OUTPUT and is not duplicated here. The trio file
# beside it is small and is tracked, since trio_validation.py reads it.
data/sv_output/novelty_filtered/hprc_multisample.trf.noveltyFiltered.tsv
